Take these two samples as column vectors:

    xs: 2 4 4 4 5 5 7 9
    ys: 1 3 5 7 9 11 13 15

Print four lines, in this order:

1. the mean of xs
2. the median of xs
3. the sample standard deviation of xs, rounded to three decimals by
   multiplying by 1000, rounding to the nearest integer, and dividing by 1000
4. the Pearson correlation of xs with ys, rounded to three decimals the same
   way

Print each value with `.` followed by `cr`, so each line holds one number.
